        "Edit image 1 in place. Image 2 is the independent assembled fabric reference, for texture and palette only. Image 3 maps the target on image 1: white is the main area, gray is the feathered transition, black is protected. Give every existing marked fabric pixel the hue, contrast and soft fabric shading from image 2, including the smallest detached patches. Match the existing silhouette and leave no breaks or background inside any fabric area. Preserve all fragment positions, outlines, seams, sizes and margin. Return image 1 as a single UV sheet.",
